| halogen-qwen3.8-flash-next | mtp | pp8192 | 8185 | 782.58 ± 98.16 | 669.3-842.0 |
| halogen-qwen3.8-flash-next | mtp | pp16384 | 16393 | 769.84 ± 46.73 | 719.2-811.4 |
| halogen-qwen3.8-flash-next | mtp | tg128 | 128 | 34.45 ± 8.84 | 15.6-44.2 |

pp = prefill (prompt processing), tg = token generation.
Both are END-TO-END over HTTP and include that request's prefill, so tg
slightly understates the pure decode rate.
tg is a MEAN OVER PROMPT SHAPES, and the min-max column is not noise: draft
acceptance depends on how predictable the text is, so code and proofs run
~2x prose. Quote the mean with the prompt set named, never a single shape.
  note: tg128 over 10 prompt shapes x 3 reps (eval-prompts.json)
